<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Get started on Termorq</title><link>https://termorq-docs.garrardkitchen.com/docs/get-started/</link><description>Recent content in Get started on Termorq</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><atom:link href="https://termorq-docs.garrardkitchen.com/docs/get-started/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Install and run</title><link>https://termorq-docs.garrardkitchen.com/docs/get-started/install/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://termorq-docs.garrardkitchen.com/docs/get-started/install/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Termorq is a desktop app. Version &lt;strong&gt;0.20.0&lt;/strong&gt; is the &lt;code&gt;version&lt;/code&gt; in &lt;code&gt;src-tauri/tauri.conf.json&lt;/code&gt;. The header, &lt;code&gt;termorq-cli --version&lt;/code&gt;, and &lt;code&gt;package.json&lt;/code&gt; read that same value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You need &lt;a href="https://nodejs.org/" rel="external" target="_blank"&gt;Node.js&lt;svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 20 or newer, &lt;a href="https://pnpm.io/" rel="external" target="_blank"&gt;pnpm&lt;svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 10, and &lt;a href="https://rustup.rs/" rel="external" target="_blank"&gt;Rust&lt;svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"&gt;&lt;path fill="currentColor" d="M14 5c-.552 0-1-.448-1-1s.448-1 1-1h6c.552 0 1 .448 1 1v6c0 .552-.448 1-1 1s-1-.448-1-1v-3.586l-7.293 7.293c-.391.39-1.024.39-1.414 0-.391-.391-.391-1.024 0-1.414l7.293-7.293h-3.586zm-9 2c-.552 0-1 .448-1 1v11c0 .552.448 1 1 1h11c.552 0 1-.448 1-1v-4.563c0-.552.448-1 1-1s1 .448 1 1v4.563c0 1.657-1.343 3-3 3h-11c-1.657 0-3-1.343-3-3v-11c0-1.657 1.343-3 3-3h4.563c.552 0 1 .448 1 1s-.448 1-1 1h-4.563z"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/a&gt; 1.90 or newer (stable). Tauri 2.12 requires that Rust version.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>The window</title><link>https://termorq-docs.garrardkitchen.com/docs/get-started/the-window/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://termorq-docs.garrardkitchen.com/docs/get-started/the-window/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The window is one prompt with a rail on the left and a header on top. Everything else, HTTP, MCP, models, and collections, opens in that same column.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;pre class="mermaid"&gt;flowchart LR
 rail[[&amp;#34;Rail&amp;#34;]]:::store
 prompt[&amp;#34;Prompt&amp;#34;]:::step
 shell[&amp;#34;Shell&amp;#34;]:::out
 http[&amp;#34;HTTP&amp;#34;]:::step
 mcp[(&amp;#34;MCP&amp;#34;)]:::store
 model{&amp;#34;Model&amp;#34;}:::gate

 rail --&amp;gt; prompt
 prompt --&amp;gt; shell
 prompt --&amp;gt; http
 prompt --&amp;gt; mcp
 prompt --&amp;gt; model

 classDef store fill:#134e4a,stroke:#5eead4,stroke-width:2px,color:#f4fbfa
 classDef gate fill:#FFC131,stroke:#b45309,stroke-width:2px,color:#1a1404
 classDef step fill:#0f766e,stroke:#99f6e4,stroke-width:2px,color:#f4fbfa
 classDef out fill:#155e75,stroke:#67e8f9,stroke-width:2px,color:#f4fbfa
 linkStyle 0,1,2 stroke:#5eead4,stroke-width:2.5px
 linkStyle 3 stroke:#67e8f9,stroke-width:2.5px
 linkStyle 4 stroke:#FFC131,stroke-width:2.5px
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;h2 id="the-rail"&gt;The rail &lt;a href="#the-rail" class="anchor" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;i class="material-icons align-middle"&gt;link&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;The rail is 64 pixels wide. Each button has a label and a tooltip.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Sample workspace</title><link>https://termorq-docs.garrardkitchen.com/docs/get-started/sample-workspace/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://termorq-docs.garrardkitchen.com/docs/get-started/sample-workspace/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;The &lt;a href="https://termorq-docs.garrardkitchen.com/docs/get-started/sample-workspace/#download"&gt;download&lt;/a&gt; is the workspace the &lt;code&gt;termorq-cli&lt;/code&gt; chapter already runs. It contains no token. &lt;code&gt;mock://users&lt;/code&gt; answers on this machine, so the HTTP steps need no network.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unpack it, then point &lt;code&gt;termorq-cli&lt;/code&gt; at the folder with an absolute path. A relative &lt;code&gt;.&lt;/code&gt; is rejected.&lt;/p&gt;


 
 &lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#d8dee9;background-color:#2e3440;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;termorq-cli list --workspace ~/src/acme-apis
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;termorq-cli show Smoke --workspace ~/src/acme-apis
&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;termorq-cli check Smoke --workspace ~/src/acme-apis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;termorq-cli check&lt;/code&gt; exits 2 until you set &lt;code&gt;AIT_SECRET_USERS_API&lt;/code&gt;. The value can be any non-empty string for this demo. The app masks it as &lt;code&gt;••••••••&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>